<title>GERMANY: GERMAN DATA DUE - BME/Reuters PMI on June 2.</title>
<headline>GERMAN DATA DUE - BME/Reuters PMI on June 2.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The BME/Reuters German Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) for May will be released on June 2 at 0730 GMT.</p>
<p>The index, which was launched last month, stood at a seasonally-adjusted level of 56.58 in April compared with 54.58 in March, reaching the highest reading yet recorded.</p>
<p>On an unadjusted basis, the index also hit a record of 57.93, up from 56.43 in March.</p>
<p>A reading of the PMI above 50 indicates the manufacturing economy is expanding.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
